# Write change notes

<h2 id="know-who-can-see-change-notes">Know who can see change notes</h2>

Anyone can read a change note, and it may be emailed to people who follow the page. Leave out names, addresses and anything private.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Fixed the lock help after Sam’s lock failed at 14 Elm Road. | Clarified what happens when a lock does not report a new state. |

<h2 id="wg-091">Say what changed and why it matters</h2>

Write a note when a meaning, a step or a result changed. Say what it means for the household. Put the key point first, name the page, card or section, and use full sentences. Do not write one for a typo, layout or a fixed link.

Good change notes:

- Clarified that a lock can take a few seconds to report its new state.
- Changed “Switch” to “Turn on” on the hall light card so the label matches the action.

Poor change notes:

- Updated the page.
- Changed some labels.
- Made improvements to the dashboard help.
